{"versions":[{"path":"versions/00d2d5b8-c0ed-4187-9456-0429e91f844a/1d395b12b9afe159106c009c3da205ffbbd1106166933eff88c275e8ed373dcd.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"00d2d5b8-c0ed-4187-9456-0429e91f844a","revision":"sha256:1d395b12b9afe159106c009c3da205ffbbd1106166933eff88c275e8ed373dcd","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"The height of an empty tree is defined to be −1, and the height of a single-node tree is 0. The minimum possible number of nodes in an AVL tree of height 4 is 12."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"ad9b515c-eadc-4cf7-9b94-bde28521c008"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"f5c7a277-f7a3-49b0-aa3e-61faa5fa0e92"}]}}},{"path":"versions/d9bdc245-ddd9-4b1f-94d2-7d5d977b391d/d44324ce9142904419ef02d42dbc2fcb2f9da8aa409089bf220b19ecb1fe651e.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"d9bdc245-ddd9-4b1f-94d2-7d5d977b391d","revision":"sha256:d44324ce9142904419ef02d42dbc2fcb2f9da8aa409089bf220b19ecb1fe651e","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"An initially empty stack supports Push and MultiPop(k), where $k$ is a nonnegative integer.\n\n\n- Push inserts one element and has actual cost $1$.\n- MultiPop(k) removes $r=\\min(k,s)$ elements and has actual cost $r$, where $s$ is the stack size before the operation.\n\nAll other costs are ignored. The amortized cost of operation $i$ is defined as\n\n$\\hat{c}_i=c_i+\\Phi_i-\\Phi_{i-1},$\n\nwhere $c_i$ is the actual cost and $\\Phi_i$ is the potential after operation $i$.\n\nStatement: With the potential function $\\Phi=s$, where $s$ is the current stack size, a MultiPop operation that removes $r$ elements has amortized cost $0$, and the total amortized cost is an upper bound on the total actual cost for every legal operation sequence starting from the empty stack."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"2a2fbfc7-cd48-4a93-88ec-64537091aa17"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"462695de-71a7-4397-b04d-96f21fbc3636"}]}}},{"path":"versions/15e8ebe6-cfa7-43fa-9043-737251496e6e/3581bba60dec15b530bfa54bf7129f212ea63404ea51d6be7423090d69395ba5.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"15e8ebe6-cfa7-43fa-9043-737251496e6e","revision":"sha256:3581bba60dec15b530bfa54bf7129f212ea63404ea51d6be7423090d69395ba5","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Removing Property (2) (“the root is black”) while keeping the other four red-black properties does not guarantees that the longest path from the root to a NIL leaf is at most twice the shortest path."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":false,"option_id":"3b44721b-bbbb-4b82-a70d-6aaf6c8b8891"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":true,"option_id":"0e7c03c8-d4c8-4eec-9b1e-df39be1ec3b1"}]}}},{"path":"versions/08639d9c-3057-45f3-8ba0-51365f081115/aa3f5c0318647fae79b13ca37adabff30ab05758374fdd795c1f1fc3636aeb55.json","value":{"schema_version":1,"revision_scheme":"holly-question-v1","bank_id":"3eb3811b-4425-46ad-8bb6-a0504dca151b","question_id":"08639d9c-3057-45f3-8ba0-51365f081115","revision":"sha256:aa3f5c0318647fae79b13ca37adabff30ab05758374fdd795c1f1fc3636aeb55","kind":"mcqs","content":{"question":[{"type":"text","content":"Two different B+ trees can contain the same set of records and have the same order, but differ in their internal separator keys while still being valid."}],"options":[{"type":"text","content":"True","correct":true,"option_id":"9aa25b2b-c6ea-464c-9c90-16268c7aa69d"},{"type":"text","content":"False","correct":false,"option_id":"3b21b2b0-8def-4ecb-86c1-c4b0c0b655ef"}]}}},{"path":"versions/ef731911-ef34-4d58-b118-481f43b825